,"From the output:\n","- `a == b` is `True` because `2` (integer) and `2.0` (float) have the same numerical value.\n","- `a is b` is `False` because `a` (an integer object) and `b` (a float object) are different types of objects, stored at different memory locations, even though their values are numerically equivalent.\n","- `a == c` is `True` because `a` and `c` have the same value.\n","- `a is c` is `True` because `c = a` makes `c` refer to the **exact same integer object** in memory that `a` refers to. Python often optimizes small integers by using a single object for them.\n","- `b == c` is `True` because `2.0` (float) and `2` (integer, which `c` refers to) have the same numerical value.\n","- `b is c` is `False` because `b` (a float object) and `c` (an integer object) are different objects in memory."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"HnR5qgaHe3rQ"},"source":["## CHALLENGES"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Ae2HErw9e3rQ"},"source":["#### Challenge 1"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"0pmOvKife3rQ"},"source":["Write a program which repeatedly reads numbers until the user enters \"done\". Once \"done\" is entered, print out the total, count, and average of the numbers. If the user enters anything other than a number, detect their mistake using try and except and print an error message and skip to the next number.\n","\n","    Enter a number: 4\n","    Enter a number: 5\n","    Enter a number: bad data\n","    Invalid input\n","    Enter a number: 7\n","    Enter a number: done\n","    16 3 5.333333333333333\n","    \n","[PEW] E5.1"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"41a39aaa","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1773038879536,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":13472,"user":{"displayName":"JOHN DERICK LUCERO","userId":"05562100238442439718"}},"outputId":"e94dce06-da89-42c9-847b-4e6e92cd1ed7"},"source":["total = 0\n","count = 0\n","\n","while True:\n","    num_str = input('Enter a number: ')\n","    if num_str == 'done':\n","        break\n","\n","    try:\n","        num = float(num_str)\n","        total += num\n","        count += 1\n","    except ValueError:\n","        print('Invalid input')\n","        continue\n","\n","if count > 0:\n","    average = total / count\n","    print(f'{total} {count} {average}')\n","else:\n","    print('No numbers were entered.')"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Enter a number: 4\n","Enter a number: 5\n","Enter a number: bad data\n","Invalid input\n","Enter a number: 7\n","Enter a number: done\n","16.0 3 5.333333333333333\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ts7aZrXte3rQ"},"source":["#### Challenge 2  "]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"GiUa3gnoe3rQ"},"source":["Write another program that prompts for a list of numbers as above and at the end prints out both the maximum and minimum of the numbers instead of the average.\n","\n","[PEW] E5.2"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"a1da9773","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1773038988966,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":13072,"user":{"displayName":"JOHN DERICK LUCERO","userId":"05562100238442439718"}},"outputId":"33a5f233-c3b9-4a85-c60b-979b7448eb09"},"source":["maximum = None\n","minimum = None\n","\n","while True:\n","    num_str = input('Enter a number: ')\n","    if num_str == 'done':\n","        break\n","\n","    try:\n","        num = float(num_str)\n","\n","        if maximum is None or num > maximum:\n","            maximum = num\n","\n","        if minimum is None or num < minimum:\n","            minimum = num\n","\n","    except ValueError:\n","        print('Invalid input')\n","        continue\n","\n","if maximum is not None and minimum is not None:\n","    print(f'Maximum: {maximum}')\n","    print(f'Minimum: {minimum}')\n","else:\n","    print('No numbers were entered.')"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream"